  "metadata": {
    "authors": [
      "rules-as-references conformance (esm-spec §9.6.4 rule 3)"
    ],
    "description": "esm-spec §9.6.4 rule 3, a single rewritten body that another registry entry can still reach. The match-less template `ddx` holds a spatial `D` and is called once, with `u` (declared shape [x]), so `central_1d` (scoped by `where f: shape [x]`) fires in its body and every reached instance rewrites to the same body. But the authored match-less entry `wrap` references `ddx` and nothing in the component references `wrap`: it keeps its authored body, is emitted, and joins the registry of any document that mounts or flattens this component, where a reference to it may bind a variable of another shape. So `ddx` is not rewritten in place: it keeps its authored body, the rewritten body is registered as `ddx.variant1`, and the call site is re-pointed to it. The same holds transitively: `outer` references `inner` (whose body holds the `D`), the equation for `dw` references `outer`, and the unreferenced authored entry `hidden` references `outer`; `inner` and `outer` both keep their authored bodies and gain `inner.variant1` and `outer.variant1`, the second referencing the first. A template that only reached references name is still rewritten in place (see `rewrite_in_template_body/`).",
    "name": "rewrite_shared_by_unreached_entry"
  },
